> f(x: u8) = 256 % x
  note: literal 256 does not fit u8; it becomes 0
> domain f
domain of f:
  x: u8, 0..255
  requires x != 0  (in 0 % x)
  defined at 255 of 256 points
  defined for: 1..255
  undefined e.g. at x=0
  C undefined behaviour at 1 points, e.g. x=0
  over all 256 points of the domain
> range f
range of f -> u8:
  0..0   (1 distinct values)
  values: 0
  fits in u1
  undefined at 1 points
  over all 256 points of the domain
> wrap f
wrap analysis of f:
  no wrapping or rounding operations
  end to end: equals the mathematical (unbounded) result everywhere
  over all 256 points of the domain
